 to grow at a compound annual  growth rate of 46 percent over the next  four years  to reach 3.7 billion us dollars by 2021.  now that we know the potential of this  field let's ask the question  who is a robotics engineer a robotics  engineer is someone who creates robots  to fulfill a particular need  these needs are usually things that  humans cannot do by themselves  or aren't willing to do so  so what are the skills required to  become a robotics engineer  first you will need programming skills  in javascript  python c or c plus plus java  and much more a clear understanding of  languages will help you set up  interactions with hardware  electronics and the real world with ease  you will need to be good at math and  science  algebra calculus geometry physics  applied mathematics and more to make  sure  to help create equations and formulas  to help your robot move and so on you  will need experience with  microprocessors  since they act as the necessary  components to create prototypes  and you will need experience working  with sensors  since they are used to observe the  environments around the robot  being experienced with machine learning  algorithms also can be extremely useful  for you  now let's talk about the  responsibilities of a robotics  engineer a robotics engineer designs  builds tests and maintains prototypes  you will need to design systems to  control robot systems  analyze and evaluate robot prototypes  to perform integration tests and quality  control  applying appropriate machine learning  techniques and much  more next up we have the salary of a  robotics engineer  according to glassdoor in india a  robotics engineer can earn approximately  364 000 rupees per annum  in the united states they can earn  approximately 75 000 dollars per annum  finally we have the blockchain developer  blockchain refers to a system that  enables the recording of information  in a way that's impossible to change  hack or cheat the system  it is a ledger of trans